As you will no doubt hear or read in the news over the next day, HP plans
to announce formal support for our project.  The announcement will take
place at Linux World Expo, March 1-4 in San Jose, California. We will be
on hand to answer questions, discuss the status of the port, and to
recruit new members.

HP will be providing us with extensive technical documentation on the
architecture as well as reference specifications for the peripherals.
Discussions are ongoing as to exactly which materials will be released and
under which license or waranty. 

The allocation of resources and all communications with HP will be
coordinated by us. We have been in discussions with several individuals
internally in order to help bring this about and it is quite exciting to
see formally announced.

Special thanks to Phil Schwan for working on configuring and moving the
mailing lists and CVS repository, Paul Lahaie for his work on the
cross-compiler, Jason Eckhardt for getting something booting that actually
says `Linux', and for all the words of encouragement and support which
have been coming in from all directions.

Over the next several weeks we will be looking at methods for effectively
disseminating information, specifically documentation, and for getting the
right equipment into the hands of the right developers.

 		--- Christopher Beard & Alex deVries

